mial of degree $7,$ with no terms of degree other than $7.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $1.$ It is a polynomial of degree $1,$ and all of its terms are of degree $1.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y,z)$ is  homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ and all of its terms are of degree $3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405016 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d14dbef-9a16-537e-a182-87fd6853e543" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Divergent Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0118fcd2-3fb3-5d19-8d54-74b731ba63af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472514} {:answer/id #uuid "185007ee-7759-5766-aba5-89fd735ff1d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "185007ee-7759-5766-aba5-89fd735ff1d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472515} :answer-field/id #uuid "76e1c758-f96e-5e38-a825-4534ee09d9c8" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}}{1-{n}^{2}}$ for $n\\ge 2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473652} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be82617a-5165-5619-a963-79617d0fb8a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472516} {:answer/id #uuid "a4acbd6f-94bc-50c4-8cf1-90972310c364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be82617a-5165-5619-a963-79617d0fb8a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472516} :answer-field/id #uuid "230986f1-b69c-54fe-a946-e524b56da72a" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{3}{n}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473653} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6428e025-be55-5e9d-a741-674cab46f66b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472518} {:answer/id #uuid "dfd56f4c-ce88-53f8-9163-fd06eb6824f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6428e025-be55-5e9d-a741-674cab46f66b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472518} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fcd4fcd-f673-515e-8c18-48e21edbbda3" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{2{n}^{2}-3{n}^{3}}{{n}^{3}+5}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b53e039b-59a1-50db-a9e2-e8f3ca992207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669001} {:answer/id #uuid "4cea64b3-09d7-5cde-a807-a0be445e6b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b53e039b-59a1-50db-a9e2-e8f3ca992207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669001} :answer-field/id #uuid "56849060-19a4-592c-971b-74d024c42f6e" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd4fed36-e750-5401-88f4-2ac9e7e598e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-123316" :question/problem "Which of the following sequences diverge?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each sequence in turn. We need to calculate the limit of each sequence as $n$ approaches infinity.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}}{1-{n}^{2}}$ for $n\\ge 2$”,  the dominant term in the denominator is $-{n}^{2},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}}{1-{n}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\left(\\frac{{n}^{3}}{{n}^{2}}\\right)}{(\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}-\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n}{(\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n}{0-1} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{3}{n}$ for $n\\ge 1$”, the limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{3}{n}=0.\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{2{n}^{2}-3{n}^{3}}{{n}^{3}+5}$ for $n\\ge 1$”, the dominant term in the denominator is ${n}^{3},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & =\\frac{2{n}^{2}-3{n}^{3}}{{n}^{3}+5} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2{n}^{2}}{{n}^{3}}-\\frac{3{n}^{3}}{{n}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{n}^{3}}{{n}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{n}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2}{n}-3)}{(1+\\frac{5}{{n}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-3}{1+0} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\nIn conclusion, sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}}{1-{n}^{2}}$ for $n\\ge 2$” diverges."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3fe3596-340e-5155-bed3-cf25f5843d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Two-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86eb0777-d080-53e8-b004-79a014639bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473088} {:answer/id #uuid "7872a4e4-6631-5d82-b92a-e36225c1be50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86eb0777-d080-53e8-b004-79a014639bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473088} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7455588-72d5-550c-9183-e46e0782f4aa" :answer-field/key "![Diagram I](images/53/5303e5de04148fbd414db26930d50d5c0cd4ef19af5a46afaf4b312966cdfded.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79c0d29f-bfc2-506c-909d-d2ee04efe33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473090} {:answer/id #uuid "0b1c9619-2805-5f10-9fdb-01a2befb4460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79c0d29f-bfc2-506c-909d-d2ee04efe33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473090} :answer-field/id #uuid "11293092-de1e-51d5-b24b-3326cc42091a" :answer-field/key "![Diagram II](images/cc/ccdca51aef8ee61c23d3f3a81b1e4673598ffdde88cb4f58b4b35bb76886f524.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee9299db-52e0-589b-b002-e37948bbdadf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473092} {:answer/id #uuid "474e300d-b0ad-520c-b70a-93c1e5e2e177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9299db-52e0-589b-b002-e37948bbdadf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473092} :answer-field/id #uuid "19219c0d-23df-589d-82c4-a37e066f5d0f" :answer-field/key "![Diagram III](images/e4/e495be81f41917740b46b1bfd43fd5cde69041981463c3dbbd96e55d206a8806.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473941} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6257fe4e-839a-565a-8b2c-f714a654f8e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669177} {:answer/id #uuid "6345f7b4-6ad0-50c1-bece-b8d368359b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6345f7b4-6ad0-50c1-bece-b8d368359b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669178} :answer-field/id #uuid "57d88627-fcc0-5ab9-8ab9-960f9a4986ee" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "befb255b-f1bd-5c00-bc58-981c00e76ebb" :question/math-academy-id "q-35574" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace.  In this case we also have that the vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71f417cf-0536-54c4-b46a-510edd2f3084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472814} {:answer/id #uuid "74f27fa9-e14e-5a7b-a59d-e4f8f4f07523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71f417cf-0536-54c4-b46a-510edd2f3084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472814} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c82116e-ddf7-523c-8827-05efd60ca46b" :answer-field/key "If $-2\\notin Z,$ then $5$ is not prime." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473802} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fb3e374-acff-5951-8e7b-106d3ee1d226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604549