ent :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "879c0bb5-661f-591a-9f87-49fc9ee4c018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669159} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e90d464-c485-59a8-b236-772aefacd6da" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669379}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46d6b627-57fc-5c4f-9c8a-dc31a7241e7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334252" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{1}(x)=x$ is a solution to the equation” is true. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =1 \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}(0)-x(1)+x & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{2}$ is a solution to the equation” is false. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =2x \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}(2)-x(2x)+{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is not a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation” is false. Since ${y}_{2}(x)$ is not a solution of the given differential equation, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ don't form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${y}_{1}(x)=x$ is a solution to the equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d074dea2-9b08-51ae-a12c-baf0473ca84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474626} {:answer/id #uuid "0745ed52-86ba-5e86-a9f5-e70229ac22d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d074dea2-9b08-51ae-a12c-baf0473ca84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474626} :answer-field/id #uuid "be2ebc52-7384-5d75-816e-60c49a6a2fe5" :answer-field/key "$A⊄B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf4b3440-fc76-5da9-8a1a-101b60935d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474628} {:answer/id #uuid "6b07da64-c759-539c-8822-0100ac81394d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf4b3440-fc76-5da9-8a1a-101b60935d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474628} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0c4e0ec-4e6b-5624-b84a-752ef7179b7c" :answer-field/key "$|A|\\ne |B|$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475240} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7dd4394-62d9-59bb-a2a5-c6d2cefe8b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474630} {:answer/id #uuid "4763b50f-c918-5bd1-93e4-4aa362986b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7dd4394-62d9-59bb-a2a5-c6d2cefe8b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474630} :answer-field/id #uuid "5844b7a0-ee09-5afb-98cc-df9699b3870d" :answer-field/key "$A⊇B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475241} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb8ad267-fb53-561e-ae81-39c39f17a2af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669139} {:answer/id #uuid "ee8117c9-3e2c-5e1e-9dee-edbd5ce87e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee8117c9-3e2c-5e1e-9dee-edbd5ce87e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669140} :answer-field/id #uuid "779aeabc-aea6-5d6d-992b-ed213cf28693" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c07a7ee-9fb6-5236-b864-38ec61e9b0cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-214241" :question/problem "Which of the following are equivalence relations on $P(N)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- The relation \"$⊄$\" is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric since ${2,3}⊄{2}$ but ${2}⊂{2,3}.$\n\n- The relation \"$\\ne $\" for the cardinalities of sets is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive since $|{2}|=|{2}|.$\n\n- The relation \"$⊇$\" is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric since $N⊇{1}$ but ${1}⊉N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e4c7950-28e5-5f87-b20d-5cd3ddc396fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474632} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ca370f-8fd4-5122-9efc-7caeca9460d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e4c7950-28e5-5f87-b20d-5cd3ddc396fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474632} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd1bd756-3043-5134-837d-147e1313e4e1" :answer-field/key "$A\\,R\\,B$ if $A\\cap B