field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72fa77bc-6d37-516a-bc08-8cef3db1618e" :question/math-academy-id "q-214252" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $N.$\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,y∤x\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is not reflexive. For example, $3∣3.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not symmetric. For example, $9∤3$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not transitive. For example, $3∤2$ and $2∤9,$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not an equivalence relation since it's neither reflexive nor symmetric nor transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6302f81d-4834-56a5-b014-0a97c3dccd6f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About General Solutions of Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4049eacb-f333-5928-be15-ad4db6bd4e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474308} {:answer/id #uuid "35601916-369e-51fe-abf4-791c123c637e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35601916-369e-51fe-abf4-791c123c637e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474309} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b95782b-8b17-5f77-9801-8a99d11ccf2a" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475080} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b8d5ec7-084e-5c9f-8f80-d0e39dff32c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474310} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e17bc7-fee0-5214-bbe1-e420ad24d8df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b8d5ec7-084e-5c9f-8f80-d0e39dff32c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474310} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a78c060-c106-55f9-a38d-38117b0a316f" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{4}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45cf437a-d3e6-5bff-a122-cc094f36db9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474312} {:answer/id #uuid "91b92ce5-41cb-5b8f-8a7e-42023c7326d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45cf437a-d3e6-5bff-a122-cc094f36db9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474312} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc403eaf-5b3a-598a-b3ae-28f5e22f4037" :answer-field/key "The general solution of the equation is $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70e7263c-5b08-5b3d-9dec-3122e3a76147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669029} {:answer/id #uuid "1edc2164-4af9-50e7-bd0a-c9e35b34ec64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70e7263c-5b08-5b3d-9dec-3122e3a76147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669029} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdced459-bca1-5376-ad85-fcf1b5f948d1" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70cf3885-2e2c-5971-b49c-1988c3e0bb2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130004" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}-2y=0,$ where $x>0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\left(\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\right)+2x\\left(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}=0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is a solution to the equation” is true.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =12{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(12{x}^{2})+2x(4{x}^{3})-2{x}^{4}=18{x}^{4}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{4}$ is a solution to the equation” is false.\n\n- So, ${y}_{1}$ is a solution but ${y}_{2}$ is not a solution of the equation, hence $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$ is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement “The general solution of the equation is $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421821 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6302f81d-4834-56a5-b014-0a97c3dccd6f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About General Solutions of Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4025a2da-8220-50a7-b4f3-219e6d29cc87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474302} {:answer/id #uuid "91c226a9-4c73-5b94-92b0-1a733df3a834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4025a2da-8220-50a7-b4f3-219e6d29cc87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474302} :answer-field/id #uuid "f318ba66-ccb9-5f8e-9231-0f5fb32052aa" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=x{e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb83e9ac-cb3a-5dc7-8842-0118c6b9c9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474304} {:answer/id #uuid "74a023e8-6ba2-5b3f-a47a-189a8481e140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74a023e8-6ba2-5b3f-a47a-189a8481e140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474305} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf5c45ac-f6f4-5fdf-87b6-c55e5d17a5ea" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab0e9691-308c-596d-9c85-fd9d5dd60a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474306} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2a6d79-cf64-517d-a658-e230018451ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab0e9691-308c-596d-9c85-fd9d5dd60a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474306} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a04d4f0-4217-55ed-ab79-e4478a4fd20e" :answer-field/key "The general solution of the equation is $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d74bd09b-264f-5634-8054-3f1c70f9d9bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669027} {:answer/id #uuid "f6925548-e106-5d17-ba52-3285a65522e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d74bd09b-264f-5634-8054-3f1c70f9d9bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669027} :answer-field/id #uuid "08494236-2896-5a39-9689-fad6beba874e" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fd65812-f6ae-584d-bfe8-d11797aed930" :question/math-academy-id "q-130000" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}-4y=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =(1+x){e}^{x} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =(2+x){e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n(2+x){e}^{x}-4(x{e}^{x})=(2-3x){e}^{x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{1}(x)=x{e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation” is false.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =2{e}^{2x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n4{e}^{2x}-4{e}^{2x}=0.\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation” is true.\n\n- So, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution while ${y}_{2}$ is a solution of the equation, hence $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$ is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement “The general solution of the equation is $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b14560-29f9-58fc-ac65-5505987579fb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Situations That Can Be Modeled as a Discrete Uniform Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b14ecc36-432b-56ec-87ab-282eea355b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475002} {:answer/id #uuid "d834568e-ce97-583c-8040-fc4e266d52c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b14ecc36-432b-56ec-87ab-282eea355b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475002} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdad22ae-e385-521b-b788-7347685ca5ee" :answer-field/key "The temperature of a town on a certain day." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475427} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12cca481-ff11-55c7-91de-86d18673b2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475004} {:answer/id #uuid "e8dfccef-97df-539d-8b11-97c54d234ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12cca481-ff11-55c7-91de-86d18673b2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475004} :answer-field/id #uuid "00c49dca-0d5f-5b4f-bddf-bbbd54a75e97" :answer-field/key "The number of letters of a word randomly selected from an English dictionary." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09154e84-c363-5ed7-a1c0-e945e77a7a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475006} {:answer/id #uuid "6cd75d4f-b796-573f-80aa-522e963beda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09154e84-c363-5ed7-a1c0-e945e77a7a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475006} :answer-field/id #uuid "044a1424-5108-5da5-9fee-69fd6070dd31" :answer-field/key "The number of typos in a randomly selected book." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1827c602-dc10-5f0b-bb41-7129ca6232dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669245} {:answer/id #uuid "64621feb-3d50-5f5c-988a-56783c9994d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64621feb-3d50-5f5c-988a-56783c9994d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669246} :answer-field/id #uuid "d02368f7-fc2f-507d-b148-7b4e978bf081" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "239e34ce-3c73-5bae-b143-3d41bff8bf51" :question/math-academy-id "q-97754" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We can use the discrete uniform distribution to model the outcome of a single event when the support $S$ is finite, and each $x\\in S$ is equally likely.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The temperature of a town on a certain day” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because a temperature is a real number, so the support is not finite.\n\n- Random variable “The number of letters of a word randomly selected from an English dictionary” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. Each outcome is not equally likely (there are more short words than very long words, for example).\n\n- Random variable “The number of typos in a randomly selected book” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because the number of typos can be any positive integer. Moreover, each outcome is not equally likely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157307 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a25bce44-98ca-54c6-a59f-b7508880d5ba" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Number is Divisible by 4"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dca59057-55b3-5c7c-ba82-222cb932dc6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474314} {:answer/id #uuid "342f9c82-98c2-5afb-b7a9-9344138494ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921