{:answer/id #uuid "35fcb43b-2ff4-5503-984d-99e164dc29df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40345fa1-c3d3-53cb-8cf6-d2c039bdf5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474808} :answer-field/id #uuid "46a9bde4-82ff-51bf-855f-089dad897c86" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a09504a-aaeb-52d7-9d8c-a81678aaf58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669175} {:answer/id #uuid "787adb65-ade8-5bd7-8a01-07f00906da56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a09504a-aaeb-52d7-9d8c-a81678aaf58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669175} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eb0e92a-5ba9-5fe8-87ee-76c3888a0a11" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46f6694f-8103-554b-a6d3-9a98e8c2973d" :question/math-academy-id "q-34711" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+5{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent” is false, while statements “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” and “The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1ed11d6-e65c-5d13-bf39-31eeca3f4a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474774} {:answer/id #uuid "9628809f-61f4-5b0b-be43-73a2d17c5845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1ed11d6-e65c-5d13-bf39-31eeca3f4a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474774} :answer-field/id #uuid "cca6563a-d8d2-55ed-8656-9999204ed40f" :answer-field/key "${D}_{1}(y)={y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f41c909f-4dc5-5044-876a-c9cde7a61ff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474776} {:answer/id #uuid "928a80de-78d5-5056-b57e-bb3af260f38c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "928a80de-78d5-5056-b57e-bb3af260f38c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474777} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f5e59f-c6cc-5d49-a8d0-669dc55d7901" :answer-field/key "${D}_{2}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b00f23b-f729-5d20-a0df-805e10752102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474778} {:answer/id #uuid "14c5ee9a-b2d0-589f-a7c1-2be947c3bd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b00f23b-f729-5d20-a0df-805e10752102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474778} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca101782-ce64-5ba0-9c47-eb42bff93628" :answer-field/key "${D}_{3}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475315} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ee5db1c-8510-54cf-ba47-296429aa9ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669165} {:answer/id #uuid "82284808-d2cd-58dc-aff3-3ea6cda1a482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ee5db1c-8510-54cf-ba47-296429aa9ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669165} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc37b877-d6f3-5319-9d14-3ef561c2da94" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d7d4653-1949-5012-bba8-de86196b5589" :question/math-academy-id "q-337766" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the first term is ${y}^{2},$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=x,{f}_{1}(x)=-2x,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=3.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the second term is $y,$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${D}_{2}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7300934-7325-58fc-b00f-7f3c820f4904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474780} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd87543-a3d8-5ab5-8243-86e605cdd362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cd87543-a3d8-5ab5-8243-86e605cdd362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474781} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7d01fed-922a-532a-b59b-9c317d62c9b1" :answer-field/key "${D}_{1}(y)=3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c53b9f19-4219-5a80-980b-d117593be475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474782} {:answer/id #uuid "6086ec45-8d73-5327-9bf6-b351964b8ec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c53b9f19-4219-5a80-980b-d117593be475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474782} :answer-field/id #uuid "adc3dd8e-00ac-5bf8-8b62-c54d163b4608" :answer-field/key "${D}_{2}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b661da6-09cd-592a-b6a2-18a16a84dd92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474784} {:answer/id #uuid "24905b70-4e0e-576e-9d3b-a54bf6455c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24905b70-4e0e-576e-9d3b-a54bf6455c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474785} :answer-field/id #uuid "08616a93-0dea-5f68-a402-e3a664f40494" :answer-field/key "${D}_{3}(y)={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475318} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a43c267a-a43a-5169-a76c-44f3410653b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669167} {:answer/id #uuid "8b14bc6e-a97e-57b6-9561-a04230f112f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a43c267a-a43a-5169-a76c-44f3410653b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669167} :answer-field/id #uuid "8df83baa-180c-5c3b-8570-8c0de9df3116" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d74a3e3c-e2b0-50fc-9e27-1744209e35b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-337767" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)=3$ and ${f}_{0}(x)={x}^{2}.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the second term is $y,$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a third-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}(x)={x}^{2},{f}_{2}(x)=0,{f}_{1}(x)=-1,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${D}_{1}(y)=3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}y$; ${D}_{3}(y)={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e60bc4-ae61-5c39-ad80-14e0cdab14da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3776bd7-7901-5119-8781-5fa760852de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474248} {:answer/id #uuid "34be4cdd-980d-5cf7-afb5-69444aae9cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3776bd7-7901-5119-8781-5fa760852de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474248} :answer-field/id #uuid "6957b9f5-0c7f-5370-ba38-a21eb5e797aa" :answer-field/key "$v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475050} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3467e4a5-c790-515b-90e9-e9524b6b5643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474250} {:answer/id #uuid "b70cee36-191b-582b-b0d3-c85411adf943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3467e4a5-c790-515b-90e9-e9524b6b5643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474250} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6d9e9f8-9da1-55b6-8112-a9793448ac85" :answer-field/key "$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475051} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95bccbcb-3a47-5abe-9fa0-82e49506d42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474252} {:answer/id #uuid "270c3557-fa11-5a21-934d-4213ed1483bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "270c3557-fa11-5a21-934d-4213ed1483bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474253} :answer-field/id #uuid "0801da56-074b-503c-9458-9eeace399eb8" :answer-field/key "$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca649da9-166a-58b1-823f-c76ac7f4d50f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668985} {:answer/id #uuid "07d0c144-0d63-5d87-af2f-ab3967750f2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca649da9-166a-58b1-823f-c76ac7f4d50f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668985} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ad5df23-5d72-5dce-8ffb-7821196f84fb" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "72a34fdf-b3e5-500c-96f3-76e3e66d1191" :question/math-academy-id "q-109572" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A-2I:$\n\n$$\nA-2I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Again, since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $x$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{v}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-2I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $3$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is “$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70b9be53-9395-5371-8ad7-e19949adab26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474398} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6a58fa-bdda-5f09-9d94-437b257bb9a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70b9be53-9395-5371-8ad7-e19949adab26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474398} :answer-field/id #uuid "c83dbd2a-d3c6-528a-8958-f6e5c019702d" :answer-field/key "$max({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{11},\\mu )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3824ed15-0a45-5def-b485-9e17437c3843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474400} {:answer/id #uuid "32980db4-466c-5aff-abb2-12ee818d5f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32980db4-466c-5aff-abb2-12ee818d5f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474401} :answer-field/id #uuid "599d78d3-13a7-5faa-b23f-82c826f49593" :answer-field/key "$min({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{10},\\sigma )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475126} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60ef7010-3c1d-51c9-886d-e031be64e3c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474402} {:answer/id #uuid "badcd2b2-3071-557b-b92e-a8403da30f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ef7010-3c1d-51c9-886d-e031be64e3c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474402} :answer-field/id #uuid "482caa84-5ca9-5d2c-85ff-33b19e0b8321" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{11}}{{\\mu }^{2}+{\\sigma }^{2}+1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbf26adc-0671-5f10-a2e6-6890f6cd8b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669061} {:answer/id #uuid "d515cbfb-0c52-5297-861a-b813f80cd907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbf26adc-0671-5f10-a2e6-6890f6cd8b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669061} :answer-field/id #uuid "c97f1ca5-2d7a-519d-a75c-32001b2e06f9" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "673ddc27-8133-50ba-9995-aed461126acc" :question/math-academy-id "q-143551" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{11}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ is unknown and $\\sigma $ is known, which of the following are statistics?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression.\n\n- Expression $max({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{11},\\mu )$ is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\n- Expression $min({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{10},\\sigma )$ is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{11}$ and the *known* population standard deviation $\\sigma $ only. Note that a statistic doesn't need to include every sample element.\n\n- Expression $\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{11}}{{\\mu }^{2}+{\\sigma }^{2}+1}$ is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $min({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{10},\\sigma )$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e777d0d0-dd29-578c-afe8-acb03722065a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474356} {:answer/id #uuid "091df9c9-cbb1-5c16-be7d-f36f5c49791b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "091df9c9-cbb1-5c16-be7d-f36f5c49791b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474357} :answer-field/id #uuid "77690c3c-9b2f-5d87-9563-d49c973c00ff" :answer-field/key "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{X}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=6}^{10}{X}_{i}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59bcc66-5190-5205-ad14-54a9ec55e8cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474358} {:answer/id #uuid "bf27c658-172e-5ec5-b42e-682082363ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d59bcc66-5190-5205-ad14-54a9ec55e8cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474358} :answer-field/id #uuid "53247d84-9f2d-51fa-beee-fa05f3f84dcb" :answer-field/key "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}\\sqrt{{X}_{i}^{2}-{\\sigma }^{2}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c12a3fa8-7b5c-5de8-a3ac-a97aecf79e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474360} {:answer/id #uuid "eb125691-6204-5b53-a91f-e00cf52d68a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c12a3fa8-7b5c-5de8-a3ac-a97aecf79e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474360} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f2eaa29-a361-59a9-9859-74c9e9186b9b" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{10}}{2}+\\mu $" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9576ab65-f806-5e9b-a22a-398a36876796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669051} {:answer/id #uuid "6efb55bd-639f-5f08-80f2-4baae66fba2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9576ab65-f806-5e9b-a22a-398a36876796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669051} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4ccdc34-02ed-55ad-8278-1600e1d24912" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d216f49f-dbd6-5da5-81b2-ff39a5445339" :question/math-academy-id "q-139833" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{10}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both unknown, which of the following are statistics?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression. \n\n- Expression ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{X}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=6}^{10}{X}_{i}$ is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{10}$ only.\n\n- Expression ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}\\sqrt{{X}_{i}^{2}-{\\sigma }^{2}}$ is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$\n\n- Expression $\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{10}}{2}+\\mu $ is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{X}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=6}^{10}{X}_{i}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7112c714-4962-5b16-8f8d-765d0369b202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474460} {:answer/id #uuid "7adf6cf4-eabd-52b6-b653-73e0cbfd7368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7adf6cf4-eabd-52b6-b653-73e0cbfd7368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474461} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd78636a-3835-5942-a3fd-7e0ee14f45cb" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6df957d-bb38-5c53-b163-e6870f5cb3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474462} {:answer/id #uuid "91041c6e-f542-5d01-8196-02c9d9d65543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6df957d-bb38-5c53-b163-e6870f5cb3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474462} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa8eed09-27d9-5e21-8524-a1932ae87109" :answer-field/key "$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb30a766-7900-5d50-86d5-89016ad059f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474464} {:answer/id #uuid "02928f92-aad5-5cb3-9006-996e38c094f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02928f92-aad5-5cb3-9006-996e38c094f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474465} :answer-field/id #uuid "76d43ab0-6331-5687-9312-3d01a7f01c93" :answer-field/key "$a$ is a local maximum of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475158} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04af98d5-8515-56cb-a3e2-5ee37ec215bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669083} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9fcc26-40ff-566e-93ef-9dee590d36b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04af98d5-8515-56cb-a3e2-5ee37ec215bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669083} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe77801c-5568-5d2a-8fde-27612dd3f3c0" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ec0f059-837e-5e3d-9bb4-8d292f2af4e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163781" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈5+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, let's recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=8$” is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-3$ and\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}|=8.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite” is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-3<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}|=8>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is negative-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a local maximum of $f$” is true. Since the matrix $A$ is negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local maximum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=8$”; “$a$ is a local maximum of $f$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32262a1a-bff1-5e94-bcd1-5c7a732a6c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474466} {:answer/id #uuid "27511163-3eb0-5da9-82e4-484d6fa22922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27511163-3eb0-5da9-82e4-484d6fa22922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474467} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffb89c92-951f-50df-b288-923f96cabf37" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=2$ and $det(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45d4031d-2906-5c4f-9490-f1fa02c297d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474468} {:answer/id #uuid "f7192339-db35-51bd-a918-939ffb27ef8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45d4031d-2906-5c4f-9490-f1fa02c297d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474468} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca732c93-4b1e-5d49-a724-0ecdb3340ab3" :answer-field/key "$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bb810d3-ff1a-5452-b8a4-17bfa2b2c0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474470} {:answer/id #uuid "a060bed7-c467-5f14-8795-41afe76eb093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bb810d3-ff1a-5452-b8a4-17bfa2b2c0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474470} :answer-field/id #uuid "f14f34e2-c714-5326-9b9d-13f4ad52f6ef" :answer-field/key "$a$ is a saddle point of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475161} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34401324-7221-599b-83e6-30b590e3b042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669085} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c30bd4-a4c1-54c7-9f03-08b322e3219b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34401324-7221-599b-83e6-30b590e3b042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669085} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7689d2-bcb1-5c55-ab63-bdc0bacd53a2" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "65b2f5b4-89e0-551f-a08f-1b697ac55d76" :question/math-academy-id "q-163786" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈-2+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, we recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=2$ and $det(A)=3$” is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=2$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2)-1(1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite” is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=2>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=2>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=3>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is positive-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a saddle point of $f$” is false. Since the matrix $A$ is positive-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local minimum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{11}=2$ and $det(A)=3$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7ce264d-034d-56ae-8c45-60644fea8382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474454} {:answer/id #uuid "b69543a5-9507-55c8-9d7b-79018308daff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b69543a5-9507-55c8-9d7b-79018308daff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474455} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8218bbf-3c1e-52b2-9907-9353e67b32bb" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=1$ and $det(A)=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475153} {:a