 :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deb3a190-ad75-51f2-b3bf-7fb707355179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669081} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc6becd7-7ffb-5f16-83eb-a642ed650091" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6771fc8-6834-5ff6-940e-46f1464b61f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-163778" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈-1+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, let's recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=1$ and $det(A)=4$” is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=1$ and\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|=4.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is positive-definite” is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=1>0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|=4>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is positive-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a local maximum of $f$” is false. Since the matrix $A$ is positive-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local minimum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{11}=1$ and $det(A)=4$”; “$A$ is positive-definite” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434764 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cde007a9-b0f6-57f6-b8c8-569dc617a887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474472} {:answer/id #uuid "14c4e553-7773-5d04-9993-af7dbd1b9557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cde007a9-b0f6-57f6-b8c8-569dc617a887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474472} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1bb8b62-465b-5b82-ba1a-9d8aa323116d" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=-1$ and $det(A)=-15$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475162} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9de572aa-0428-548c-97f5-19930fcda97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474474} {:answer/id #uuid "ce46449c-5f4c-5219-ada2-0e7076d87668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9de572aa-0428-548c-97f5-19930fcda97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474474} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6b0b738-bbb1-59b2-9af2-7625e85552c1" :answer-field/key "$A$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475163} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c962c53-221d-56e5-a7ba-4a50b74f26e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474476} {:answer/id #uuid "10fdc2c8-4482-572b-a145-9384b2579ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c962c53-221d-56e5-a7ba-4a50b74f26e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474476} :answer-field/id #uuid "28245267-c604-5f8b-af0e-e69a56ca6fbc" :answer-field/key "$a$ is a local minimum of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475164} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0469c806-bf58-512f-b5a9-49fdbcaf70ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669087} {:answer/id #uuid "77b9ba77-8595-5f92-a5c3-359e0fa1fe38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77b9ba77-8595-5f92-a5c3-359e0fa1fe38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669088} :answer-field/id #uuid "02514380-2789-5254-aca9-8c6ca8f0be3d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e5518b1c-8ee2-55b4-900e-3e5d5d3b8c0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-163788" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈1+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, we recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=-1$ and $det(A)=-15$” is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-1,$ but\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1(3)-4(4)+2(-6) \\\\  & =-31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is negative-definite” is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-1<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-19<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-31<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a local minimum of $f$” is false. Since the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a saddle point of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172005 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "747b25be-ff4e-5b1e-abcc-5edd1edd9790" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Situations That Can Be Modeled Using an Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "578d1446-5ed6-5cf1-883d-281def033764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474984} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b75ec3-a9af-5dd5-83ec-1c474a39eb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8b75ec3-a9af-5dd5-83ec-1c474a39eb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474985} :answer-field/id #uuid "72026fcd-17a5-58ea-baa5-60e8dca7e6fa" :answer-field/key "The execution time, in seconds, of a computer program" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475418} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19d5d9dc-11b6-5304-a9fc-92bcf20f5947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474986} {:answer/id #uuid "6513a9f4-c449-51ce-8843-4571efbf8c0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19d5d9dc-11b6-5304-a9fc-92bcf20f5947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474986} :answer-field/id #uuid "abbd9f61-d2ba-5555-b268-77fcb2dee664" :answer-field/key "The number of students in a class with blood type $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475419} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa4051b0-3e6b-5c89-8c06-f42ce6c96a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474988} {:answer/id #uuid "0b514147-01ed-5990-a394-2241fb9fcd3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa4051b0-3e6b-5c89-8c06-f42ce6c96a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474988} :answer-field/id #uuid "522cda2a-e7c7-508e-9466-5a1e387cada3" :answer-field/key "The number of books read by a student in a month" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475420} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acb15cbe-d7ce-59d1-b128-4cbc3bad4a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669243} {:answer/id #uuid "67333b85-0a5c-5e63-adcf-47ef3e0c49e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acb15cbe-d7ce-59d1-b128-4cbc3bad4a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669243} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dc42436-0452-56bc-82a6-2d64826da885" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e53ee3ed-f667-5b74-b94f-f7c404a83247" :question/math-academy-id "q-96677" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled by an exponential distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The exponential distribution can be thought of as the continuous analog of the geometric distribution. It models the amount of continuous time or space until a particular event occurs, where the events should occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The execution time, in seconds, of a computer program” could be modeled using an exponential distribution. Executions of a computer program can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know the amount of time it takes to complete a single execution.\n\n- Random variable “The number of students in a class with blood type $A$” does *not* follow an exponential distribution. There are no events that occur at a constant average rate, and there is no interval of continuous time or space. The number of students is discrete, not continuous.\n\n- Random variable “The number of books read by a student in a month” does *not* follow an exponential distribution. There is no interval of continuous time or space. The number of books is discrete, not continuous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The execution time, in seconds, of a computer program” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f564662a-a586-5cf0-983d-a463cece18c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474828} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9ec697-d62c-5cd9-a7e3-d0be9a26170b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f564662a-a586-5cf0-983d-a463cece18c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474828} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c3c4731-0b36-5964-b452-fbb2af92efe4" :answer-field/key "$M=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475340} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58c9ad47-9cc2-5588-b29e-efbaec72d300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474830} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6dd6fc-300a-5536-a4f8-6bf0bd3b7419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58c9ad47-9cc2-5588-b29e-efbaec72d300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474830} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f81fd52-e05c-55c9-8525-5b6cb62e9802" :answer-field/key "$N=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident 