t all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrices $M$, $N$ and $P$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Closed Under Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d05376f6-1b0d-5d33-a541-3aa219c70c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474380} {:answer/id #uuid "5c163f09-54be-5558-9c1e-fe94a54a1e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d05376f6-1b0d-5d33-a541-3aa219c70c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474380} :answer-field/id #uuid "40688437-da51-5c09-8938-382c42b205b5" :answer-field/key "The identity matrix ${I}_{2}$ belongs to $T.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7e8cc97-462c-55aa-b04b-6dbb38612ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474382} {:answer/id #uuid "15dd7df2-59de-5b51-b076-5c48eeebe741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7e8cc97-462c-55aa-b04b-6dbb38612ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474382} :answer-field/id #uuid "0701114c-aa2e-546e-96ef-4e5405aa562a" :answer-field/key "For every $A\\in T$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha \\cdot A\\in T.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fc0710a-c653-55e4-9d40-d1e8b67499c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474384} {:answer/id #uuid "e9124b17-545a-583b-9b07-99ee100d310e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fc0710a-c653-55e4-9d40-d1e8b67499c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474384} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce028ac2-d2da-562a-87c9-ae46090732e5" :answer-field/key "The set is closed under scalar multiplication." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7033a83c-e0ec-5727-889c-cd5887606c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669055} {:answer/id #uuid "3cffcdb6-73ae-5950-ba93-afe479f977c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cffcdb6-73ae-5950-ba93-afe479f977c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669056} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f5b820a-924c-5417-aaf1-a1eb80482a3c" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3d7a176-49a0-5f40-a976-fffa17513013" :question/math-academy-id "q-141158" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ such that ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}>0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement “The identity matrix ${I}_{2}$ belongs to $T.$” is false. The set $T$ contains only matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ such that ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}>0.$ However, for the identity matrix ${I}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},$ we have ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}=1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1=0≯0.$ So, ${I}_{2}\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement “For every $A\\in T$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha \\cdot A\\in T.$” is false. For example, let $\\alpha =0\\in R$ and $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}\\in T.$ Then, \n\n$$\n\\alpha \\cdot A=0\\cdot A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere the sum of the products of columns' entries is $0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 0=0≯0.$ Hence, $0\\cdot A\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement “The set is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since statement “For every $A\\in T$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha \\cdot A\\in T.$” is false, the set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}]
